coder › Implemented `RateLimiter` token bucket on branch `work/rate-limiter`.

What changed:
- `src/limiter.ts` — lazy-refilling token bucket: starts full (`tokens = capacity`, `last = now()`); private `refill()` adds `elapsedSeconds * refillPerSecond` capped at `capacity` on every `tryTake`/`available` access; `tryTake(n = 1)` returns `false` without consuming when `n > capacity` or `tokens < n`, else subtracts and returns `true`; `available` getter refills then returns current (possibly fractional) tokens. Kept existing constructor signature, field names, and style.
- `src/limiter.test.ts` — added 4 tests to the existing `starts full` test: multi-token take + failed take consumes nothing, continuous/fractional refill (`10` cap, `2/s`, `250ms → 0.5`), cap on refill after long idle (`60s → 3`), `n > capacity` always refused even when full.

Decisions the task did not specify:
- Refill is lazy (computed on access from `now()`), not on a timer.
- `last` only advances when time moves forward (`elapsed <= 0` is a no-op), so a clock going backward never adds or loses tokens.
- An over-capacity `tryTake` still runs the refill first (so `available` stays correct) but never consumes.

